# T-010 — M5 Release speed baseline

Implementation and standalone measurement complete, 2026-10-18. Input timings blocked by sandbox; baseline documents exact gaps and outside-sandbox rerun. Final Release build and full selftest passed; report complete.

## Implementation

- `src/AntiQuickPad/Measurement.cs`: `--measure [--samples N] [--out file.json]`, default 30 total attempts with the first 3 discarded as warmups per state (up to 27 retained), minimum 300 ms between completed cycles. Statistics are min/median/nearest-rank p95/max, with nulls for unavailable endpoints. Parent sends the real Ctrl+Alt+F9 chord and Esc through Win32 SendInput; it never substitutes internal calls for timing samples.
- Separate apphost child, unique singleton ID and unique data directory, alternate hotkey via child-only environment override. Private launch flags: `--measure-child --instance <id> --data <directory>`. No ordinary singleton acquisition in the harness; notes/settings/logs all isolated under `bin/Release/net10.0/measure/<GUID>`.
- Program dispatches measurement before ordinary residency. MainWindow probes log shared-clock events at WM_HOTKEY, foreground-confirmed editor focus, first RequestAnimationFrame callback scheduled after Show, and Hide return. Raw events include QPC ticks; parent records QPC immediately before input injection. Stopwatch.GetTimestamp at WM_HOTKEY is Windows QPC. Callback timing is explicitly not proof of paint/presentation.
- Empty-note and heavier 20-note / 200-line states in the same resident; fixture persisted through NotesSession and real editor binding. Verified on disk: 20 .md files, all 200 lines. Four 30 s idle CPU/memory windows, with 1 s settling each; control-file show/hide is only used to establish idle states. Graceful child quit plus 10-minute graceful watchdog; no process killing.
- Selftest launches a real `--measure --samples 3` child, verifies exit 0, parses JSON and requires baseline/heavy state objects, allowing explicit sandbox input gaps. It includes full idle windows (~2.5 minutes overall). Existing proof outputs redirected to the isolated selftest directory so future selftests stay under src.

## Verification and measurements

All builds used the prescribed clean exit first:

```powershell
# cwd: src/AntiQuickPad
dotnet bin/Release/net10.0/AntiQuickPad.dll --quit
$env:AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT='1'
dotnet build -c Release --no-restore -p:UseSharedCompilation=false
dotnet bin/Release/net10.0/AntiQuickPad.dll --selftest
& .\bin\Release\net10.0\AntiQuickPad.exe --measure --samples 30 --out .\measure-release.json
```

- Final Release build: exit 0, **0 warnings, 0 errors**, 2.22 s.
- Final full selftest: **exit 0**, including real `--measure --samples 3` JSON smoke, all four 30 s resource windows, editor/proof, persistence, quit, carousel and focus checks. Final internal scripted focus values 3.037 / 1.438 / 1.197 ms are not keyboard-to-visible measurements. Smoke JSON: `src/AntiQuickPad/bin/Release/net10.0/selftest/de5bae0a316d429a81dcbd328c490386/measure-smoke.json`.
- Standalone default 30-sample invocation: exit 0, child graceful exit 0, JSON written to `src/AntiQuickPad/measure-release.json` (schema 1; qpcFrequency 10,000,000; requestedSamples 30; two explicit input gaps).
- Cold process start -> startup frame callback: **952.144 ms** (single observation; prior smoke 981.445 ms).
- Idle windows (WS MiB / private MiB / CPU percent of one core): empty hidden **141.79 / 103.68 / 0.208**; empty shown **199.04 / 191.73 / 100.341**; heavy hidden **200.30 / 189.80 / 97.819**; heavy shown **201.98 / 205.34 / 97.196**. Each CPU window actually 30.007–30.014 s. High CPU after show reproduced across runs; cause unresolved, recheck on normal desktop before assuming app or sandbox cause.
- Machine: Windows build 26340.9616 / registry 26H2, Ryzen 7 7800X3D, 16 logical processors, window RenderScaling 1.0 (100%), .NET 10.0.13. Physical display refresh/GPU/RAM inventory not established (CIM Access denied).

Raw standalone child stream: `src/AntiQuickPad/bin/Release/net10.0/measure/a00a6661081941a9a361ac5c11179c41/events.jsonl`. Child shell.log under the same directory's logs folder.

## Exact gaps / manager action

SendInput **0/6**, last-error **5 (Access denied)** in both empty and heavy first warmups. Alternate Ctrl+Alt+F9 registration succeeded, error 0. No WM_HOTKEY received; no foreground-confirmed focus event. Input sampling stops on the first blocked warmup in each state; actual retained n=0 despite requested n=30. Esc is not injected without confirmed foreground focus. All input->hotkey, input->focus, input->frame-callback and Esc->hidden distributions remain null. Resource metrics still run fully. These gaps are recorded in JSON; successful harness exit does not mean timing budget passed.

**<100 ms budget UNVERIFIED**, not a pass or failure. RequestAnimationFrame is a render opportunity and can precede drawing; compositor presentation/scanout and physical keyboard transport are outside this harness's evidence.

