## New files and changed wiring

New: Core/AntiQuickPad.Core.csproj; Core.Smoke/AntiQuickPad.Core.Smoke.csproj and Program.cs; ViewModels/ObservableObject.cs (also RelayCommand), MainViewModel.cs (also navigation args/WindowSnapshot), NoteViewModel.cs, StatusViewModel.cs; Views/IShellView.cs (also IEditorHost); Shell/PlatformServices.cs and AvaloniaWindowPlatform.cs. Extracted destinations are listed above.

Changed wiring: AntiQuickPad.csproj adds the Core project reference without changing its three existing package references. App.cs constructs the graph and shell switch. Program.cs attaches IShellView and owns ISingleInstanceService; command-only quit remains before Avalonia startup. Measurement.cs accepts IShellView and uses Host for frame/foreground timing. GlobalHotkey.cs and SingleInstanceService.cs implement interfaces without changing native logic. CarouselController.cs receives MainViewModel instead of store-shaped delegates; Carousel/README.md records ownership. DesignWindow.cs implements IEditorHost; its layout/styles/fixtures remain unchanged. EditorFactory.cs calls VM text operations and adapts Core parsing.

Documentation: docs/architecture.md contains the layer diagram, dependency rule, feature map, navigation contract, offline checks and exactly five steps to add Quiet/Card without Core/VM changes. Checkpoints: .coord/status-T012.md.

